diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 7e403f0..795940a 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -30,3 +30,14 @@ Bots are `User` records with `role: :bot` (`User::Role`), implemented via the `U
   - `200` with `text/plain` (HTML-escaped so literal text renders safely) or `text/html` posts the non-blank response body into the room as the bot's message and calls `broadcast_create`.
   - `204` (or other statuses / empty body) posts nothing.
 - Outbound webhook URLs intentionally permit `http://` and `https://` on localhost and private networks (unlike `Opengraph::Fetch`) so self-hosted Campfire instances and local integrations/tests can target internal services.
+
+## Per-Member Bot Limit
+- `Account#settings` stores `bots_per_member` (integer, default `Account::DEFAULT_BOTS_PER_MEMBER = 5`) via `has_json`, validated to be a non-negative integer (`>= 0`).
+- Administrators configure `Bots per member` on `/account/edit` (non-admin members do not see or edit this setting).
+- `User::Bot#can_create_bot?` / `User::Bot#bot_limit_reached?`:
+  - Administrators (`administrator?`) are never limited.
+  - Members are capped at `bots.count < bots_per_member`, where `user.bots` already scopes to `active.bot` so deactivated/deleted bots do not count.
+  - Lowering `bots_per_member` does not deactivate existing bots; members at or above the limit can still view, edit, and delete their existing bots, and only new bot creation is blocked.
+- Enforcement:
+  - `app/views/bots/index.html.erb` hides `"Add a chat bot"` and displays `"You’ve reached the limit of ..."` when `Current.user.bot_limit_reached?`.
+  - `BotsController` enforces `before_action :ensure_can_create_bot, only: %i[ new create ]`, refusing `GET /bots/new` and `POST /bots` with `403 Forbidden` (rendering `bots/index`).
